(ns kotoba.compiler.nbb.verdict-cache
  "Persistent, content-addressed cache of STATIC VERDICTS about definitions
  (adr-2609242100 P5, first half).

  ## What it holds, and what it does not

  A verdict is `{:admitted true}` or `{:refused {:message m :data d}}` -- the
  answer a validator gave, never a value it computed and never a trust
  decision. The one validator wired to it today is compile-time
  `kotoba.verifier/verify-artifact!` in the nbb native driver (see
  `kotoba.compiler.nbb.cli`), because that is the only static verdict on the
  compile path that costs anything: measured 2026-09-24 on
  examples/recursive-tree.kotoba and examples/approval-queue-app.kotoba,
  native-verify was 1.0-3.0 s per compile, while front-end admission
  (`effect-row/check`) was 0-20 ms and native admission
  (`only-native-word-typed-features?`) 4-22 ms.

  Execution-time checks are NOT static verdicts and never pass through here:
  `amu run` / `amu verify` / `extract-native` verify signatures and artifact
  integrity on every invocation.

  ## The key

  Every input the verdict depended on, each as a named field:

    :kind          which validator (`:kotoba.verdict/native-verify`)
    :definitions   `definition-identity/cache-material` -- the ordered
                   definition CIDs and export names. A definition CID covers
                   its dependency closure (callees are sealed as
                   `[:kotoba.definition/ref <cid>]`, cycles as scc-v1 groups),
                   so a changed callee changes every caller's CID.
    :subject       the validator's own input, canonically hashed (for
                   native-verify: the whole sealed artifact map, whose seal is
                   one of its fields)
    :toolchain     `toolchain-digest`: the classpath the process actually
                   loaded -- gitlibs entries by their pinned sha path, every
                   other entry (amu's own src/ and resources/) by the bytes
                   of every file under it -- plus the Node version and
                   `compatibility/compiler-version`
    :target        the target profile keyword
    :capabilities  canonical sha256 of the capability policy in force
    :limits        sha256 of the `kotoba/lang/limits.edn` bytes on the
                   classpath (kotoba-lang `lang/limits.edn`, vendored)

  The toolchain digest is read from disk the first time a process needs it,
  not when the code was loaded; a long-lived `amu worker` whose checkout is
  edited between its start and its first native compile keys on the edited
  bytes. Restart workers after editing the compiler.

  A module without a complete definition identity is NOT cached
  (`:unkeyed`), for the reason `definition-identity/cache-material` gives: a
  partial identity is not an identity.

  ## Storage and integrity

  One file per key, `<dir>/<key>.edn`, holding the record
  `{:format :kotoba.verdict-cache/v1 :key k :key-material m :verdict v
  :digest d}`, where `d` is the canonical sha256 of `[format k m v]`. On read
  the record's `:key` must equal the requested key, the key recomputed from
  `:key-material` must equal it too, and the digest must match. Any failure
  -- unreadable, malformed, key mismatch, digest mismatch -- deletes the
  entry, prints one `kotoba.verdict-cache: rejected` line on stderr, and
  recomputes. A rejected entry is never trusted.

  The digest detects corruption and mismatch, not forgery: anyone who can
  write the directory can write a self-consistent record. Forgery is kept out
  the way `bin/amu` keeps its classpath cache: the directory must be owned by
  this uid and not group/world writable, files are opened without following
  symlinks and must be owned by this uid, and writes are 0600 temp + rename.
  A directory that fails those checks disables the cache (`:disabled`).

  ## Configuration

    KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE=off           disable
    KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_DIR           default <os.tmpdir>/amu-verdict-cache-<uid>
                                       (an empty value is unset)
    KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_ENTRIES       default 4096, at most 65536
    KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_BYTES         default 16 MiB, at most 1 GiB

  parallel to the worker's `KOTOBA_WORKER_CACHE_*` bounds.

  ## Host effects

  Every one is an ability call (superproject adr-2609242330 S5): env/read,
  hash/sha256, entropy/draw (the temporary name), io/write-error (the
  warning) and fs/app-data / fs/browse for the store. The security rules
  above are THIS module's decisions, spelled in wire-35 requests the handler
  answers one host call each:

    owner-only directory   NOFOLLOW (a directory, mode & 0o022 = 0) and
                           OWNER (owner uid = this process's euid); a missing
                           directory is created 0700 as MKTEMP in its parent,
                           then RENAMEd to its name, so it never exists with a
                           wider mode
    symlink / foreign      NOFOLLOW (a symlink is unreadable; anything but a
                           regular file, a foreign owner or a group/world
                           writable mode is :foreign-entry), then RANGE of
                           exactly that size, which does not follow a symlink
    0600 temp + rename     WRITE (empty, O_NOFOLLOW), CHMOD 600, WRITE the
                           record, RENAME -- no byte exists under another mode

  OWNER is a proposed form of wire 35 (kotoba-lang capability catalog); no
  native host answers it yet. Windows keeps its stated non-claims: no owner
  or mode check and a followed final component, as before."
  {:kotoba/export #?(:kotoba [key-for key-material limits-digest lookup-verdict open-store record-digest
                              store-verdict! toolchain-digest]
                     :default [key-for key-material limits-digest open-store record-digest
                               resolve! toolchain-digest])}
  (:require [kotoba.artifact.core :as artifact]
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.decimal-text :as decimal-text])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.posix-path :as posix-path])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.text-bytes :as text-bytes])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.kir.compatibility :as compatibility])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.lang.edn :as edn])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.lang.text :as text])
            ;; Abilities (superproject adr-2609242330 S5); `sys` holds the
            ;; host facts no ability carries.
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.entropy :as entropy])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.env :as env])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.fs :as fs])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.hash :as hash])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.io :as io])
            #?(:cljs [kotoba.compiler.nbb.host.sys :as sys])
            #?@(:kotoba [[kotoba.compiler.posix-path :as posix-path]
                         [kotoba.compiler.decimal-text :as decimal-text]
                         [kotoba.compiler.nbb.compile-cache :as digest]
                         [kotoba.kir.compatibility :as compatibility]])))

;; Kotoba reading: THE SAME STORE, WITHOUT THE CLOSURE. The identity (key,
;; record digest, key material, toolchain and limits digests) and the store
;; protocol (owner-only directory, no-follow reads, 0600 temporary + rename,
;; record/key/digest verification, a rejected entry deleted) are all here, in
;; wire-35 requests. What a Kotoba module cannot carry is `resolve!`'s
;; compute closure and its two pieces of process state, so the caller splits
;; it: `lookup-verdict` (a trusted verdict or null), then compute, then
;; `store-verdict!`. Left to the host reading, named: entry/byte eviction
;; (`evict!`), the one-line `rejected` warning on stderr, and the toolchain
;; digest of the process's own `--classpath` argv (a Kotoba module is handed
;; the entries). A raise cannot be caught on the Kotoba route, so a
;; malformed or foreign entry is a miss (and is deleted), never an abort.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn key-for [material :document] :string
     (artifact/sha256 material)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn record-digest [key :string material :document verdict :document] :string
     (artifact/sha256 (document-vector (document-keyword :kotoba.verdict-cache/v1)
                                       (document-string key) material verdict))))


;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Kotoba: key material, toolchain and limits identity, the store

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- field [m :document k :keyword] :document
     (option-value-of [:option :document] (document-get m k) (document-null))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- slot [fields :document k :keyword] :document
     (document-vector (document-keyword k) (field fields k))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn key-material
     "The ordered vector the key is the hash of: every field present, named, in
     a fixed order; an absent field is part of the material as null."
     [kind :keyword fields :document] :document
     (document-vector (document-keyword :kotoba.verdict-key/v1)
                      (document-keyword kind)
                      (document-vector (slot fields :definitions) (slot fields :subject)
                                       (slot fields :toolchain) (slot fields :target)
                                       (slot fields :capabilities) (slot fields :limits)))))

#?(:kotoba (defn- nul [] :string (string-from-utf8 (bytes-from-vector-i64 (vector-i64 0)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- file-digest [file :string] :string
     (digest/sha256-bytes (fs/app-data-bytes file))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- numbers [answer :string] :vector-i64
     (if (= 0 (string-byte-length answer))
       (vector-i64)
       (decimal-text/fields answer))))

;; `.../.gitlibs/libs/<group>/<artifact>/<40-hex sha>/...` names the commit,
;; which is the identity deps-lock.edn pins. Either separator, as the host's
;; regex [/\\]\.gitlibs[/\\]libs[/\\].+[/\\][0-9a-f]{40}([/\\]|$).
#?(:kotoba (defn- sep? [b :i64] :bool (or (= b 47) (= b 92))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- bytes-match? [bs :bytes at :i64 needle :bytes] :bool
     (if (> (+ at (bytes-count needle)) (bytes-count bs))
       false
       (loop [j 0]
         (if (>= j (bytes-count needle))
           true
           (if (= (bytes-at bs (+ at j)) (bytes-at needle j)) (recur (+ j 1)) false))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- hex40-from? [bs :bytes at :i64] :bool
     (if (> (+ at 40) (bytes-count bs))
       false
       (loop [j 0]
         (if (>= j 40)
           true
           (let [c (bytes-at bs (+ at j))]
             (if (or (and (>= c 48) (<= c 57)) (and (>= c 97) (<= c 102)))
               (recur (+ j 1))
               false)))))))

;; A separator at P, 40 hex after it, then a separator or the end.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- sha-segment-at? [bs :bytes p :i64] :bool
     (if (sep? (bytes-at bs p))
       (if (hex40-from? bs (+ p 1))
         (if (= (+ p 41) (bytes-count bs))
           true
           (sep? (bytes-at bs (+ p 41))))
         false)
       false)))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- sha-segment-from? [bs :bytes p :i64] :bool
     (if (>= p (bytes-count bs))
       false
       (if (sha-segment-at? bs p) true (sha-segment-from? bs (+ p 1))))))

;; Offset one past "<sep>.gitlibs<sep>libs<sep>", or -1.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- libs-prefix-end [bs :bytes at :i64] :i64
     (if (>= at (bytes-count bs))
       -1
       (if (sep? (bytes-at bs at))
         (if (bytes-match? bs (+ at 1) (string-to-utf8 ".gitlibs"))
           (if (sep? (bytes-at bs (+ at 9)))
             (if (bytes-match? bs (+ at 10) (string-to-utf8 "libs"))
               (if (sep? (bytes-at bs (+ at 14)))
                 (+ at 15)
                 (libs-prefix-end bs (+ at 1)))
               (libs-prefix-end bs (+ at 1)))
             (libs-prefix-end bs (+ at 1)))
           (libs-prefix-end bs (+ at 1)))
         (libs-prefix-end bs (+ at 1))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- pinned-gitlib? [entry :string] :bool
     (let [bs (string-to-utf8 entry)
           after (libs-prefix-end bs 0)]
       ;; `.+` takes at least one character before the sha segment.
       (if (< after 0) false (sha-segment-from? bs (+ after 1))))))

;; fs/browse answers NAME<TAB>D rows; a named wrapper types its result.
#?(:kotoba (defn- listing-of [d :string] :string (fs/browse d)))

;; fs/browse rows are NAME<TAB>D joined by single newlines. The sha256 of
;; every regular file under D, depth first, in the handler's bytewise name
;; order, as "file\0<rel>\0<sha256>\0" text.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- tree-text [d :string rel :string listing :string start :i64] :string
     (if (>= start (string-byte-length listing))
       ""
       (let [nl (string-find-byte listing 10 start)
             end (if (< nl 0) (string-byte-length listing) nl)
             row (string-substring listing start end)
             tab (string-find-byte row 9 0)
             name (if (< tab 0) row (string-substring row 0 tab))
             p (string-concat d (string-concat "/" name))
             r (if (= 0 (string-byte-length rel)) name (string-concat rel (string-concat "/" name)))
             kind (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat p "NOFOLLOW_SEP")))
             here (if (< (vector-count kind) 4)
                    (throw (ex-info "toolchain tree contains a non-regular file" {:path p}))
                    (if (= 1 (vector-at kind 3))
                      (tree-text p r (listing-of p) 0)
                      (if (= 0 (vector-at kind 3))
                        (string-concat "file" (string-concat (nul) (string-concat r (string-concat (nul) (string-concat (file-digest p) (nul))))))
                        ;; A symlink inside a hashed tree is refused rather
                        ;; than followed or skipped: either would let the
                        ;; digest say less than what was loaded.
                        (throw (ex-info "toolchain tree contains a non-regular file" {:path p})))))]
         (string-concat here (tree-text d rel listing (+ end 1)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- resolve-path [p :string cwd :string] :string
     (let [joined (posix-path/normalize
                   (if (= 47 (string-code-point-at p 0)) p (posix-path/join cwd p)))]
       (if (and (< 1 (string-byte-length joined)) (= 47 (string-code-point-at joined (- (string-byte-length joined) 1))))
         (string-substring joined 0 (- (string-byte-length joined) 1))
         joined))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- entry-text [entry :string cwd :string] :string
     (let [absolute (resolve-path entry cwd)
           st (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat absolute "STAT_SEP")))
           head (string-concat "entry" (string-concat (nul) (string-concat absolute (nul))))]
       (string-concat
        head
        (if (pinned-gitlib? absolute)
          (string-concat "pinned" (nul))
          (if (< (vector-count st) 4)
            (string-concat "absent" (nul))
            (if (= 0 (vector-at st 3))
              (string-concat "sha256" (string-concat (nul) (string-concat (file-digest absolute) (nul))))
              (tree-text absolute "" (listing-of absolute) 0))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- entries-text [entries :document cwd :string i :i64] :string
     (if (>= i (document-count entries))
       ""
       (string-concat
        (entry-text (option-value-of [:option :string]
                                     (document-string-value
                                      (option-value-of [:option :document] (document-vector-at entries i) (document-null)))
                                     "")
                    cwd)
        (entries-text entries cwd (+ i 1))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn toolchain-digest
     "The toolchain identity over ENTRIES (a vector of classpath entry strings;
     relative ones against CWD): gitlibs entries by their pinned sha path,
     every other entry by the bytes of every file under it, plus the compiler
     version. The text and its hash are the host's, with the runtime named
     \"kotoba\" as the host's non-Node reading does. A non-regular file in a
     hashed tree aborts, as the host's `:unavailable` does."
     [entries :document cwd :string] :string
     (digest/sha256
      (string-concat
       (string-concat "kotoba.verdict-toolchain/v2" (string-concat (nul) (string-concat "kotoba" (nul))))
       (string-concat (string-concat (document-edn-print (document-string (compatibility/compiler-version))) (nul))
                      (entries-text entries cwd 0))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- limits-from [entries :document i :i64] [:option :string]
     (if (>= i (document-count entries))
       (option-none-of [:option :string])
       (let [entry (option-value-of [:option :string]
                                    (document-string-value
                                     (option-value-of [:option :document] (document-vector-at entries i) (document-null)))
                                    "")
             file (posix-path/join entry "kotoba/lang/limits.edn")]
         (if (= "1" (fs/app-data (string-concat file "EXISTS_SEP")))
           (option-some-of [:option :string] (file-digest file))
           (limits-from entries (+ i 1)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn limits-digest
     "sha256 of the first `kotoba/lang/limits.edn` found on ENTRIES; none when
     there is none."
     [entries :document] [:option :string]
     (limits-from entries 0)))

;; -- the store ------------------------------------------------------------

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- writable-by-others? [mode :i64] :bool
     ;; mode & 0o022 <> 0: bit 1 (world write) or bit 4 (group write).
     (or (= 1 (rem (quot mode 2) 2)) (= 1 (rem (quot mode 16) 2)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- secure-dir? [dir :string] :bool
     (let [st (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat dir "NOFOLLOW_SEP")))
           who (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat dir "OWNER_SEP")))]
       (if (< (vector-count st) 4)
         false
         (if (< (vector-count who) 2)
           false
           (if (= 1 (vector-at st 3))
             (if (writable-by-others? (vector-at st 0))
               false
               (= (vector-at who 0) (vector-at who 1)))
             false))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- absent? [p :string] :bool
     (< (vector-count (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat p "STAT_SEP")))) 4)))

;; DIR (and any missing parent) as a 0700 directory: MKTEMP in the parent --
;; created 0700 by the host -- then RENAME to DIR, so DIR never exists with a
;; wider mode. A DIR another run created meanwhile is used.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- make-private-directory! [dir :string] :i64
     (let [parent (posix-path/dirname dir)
           made (if (and (not= parent dir) (absent? parent)) (make-private-directory! parent) 0)
           staged (fs/app-data (string-concat parent (string-concat "MKTEMP_SEP" ".amu-verdict-cache-")))]
       (if (= 0 (string-byte-length staged))
         (throw (ex-info "verdict cache directory could not be created" {:dir dir}))
         (if (= "1" (fs/app-data (string-concat staged (string-concat "RENAME_SEP" dir))))
           1
           (do (fs/app-data (string-concat staged "RMDIR_SEP"))
               (if (absent? dir)
                 (throw (ex-info "verdict cache directory could not be created" {:dir dir}))
                 1)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- tmpdir-from [names :document i :i64] :string
     (if (>= i (document-count names))
       "/tmp"
       (let [v (env/read (option-value-of [:option :string]
                                          (document-string-value
                                           (option-value-of [:option :document] (document-vector-at names i) (document-null)))
                                          ""))]
         (if (> (string-byte-length v) 0) v (tmpdir-from names (+ i 1)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- default-dir [] :string
     (let [t (tmpdir-from (document-edn-read "[\"TMPDIR\" \"TMP\" \"TEMP\"]") 0)
           trimmed (if (and (< 1 (string-byte-length t)) (= 47 (string-code-point-at t (- (string-byte-length t) 1))))
                     (string-substring t 0 (- (string-byte-length t) 1))
                     t)
           me (numbers (fs/app-data "/OWNER_SEP"))]
       (posix-path/join trimmed
                        (string-concat "amu-verdict-cache-"
                                       (string-from-i64 (if (< (vector-count me) 2) 0 (vector-at me 1))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn open-store
     "The verdict-cache directory to use, or \"\" when the cache is disabled
     (KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE=off, or a directory that is not ours / is
     group- or world-writable, as the host's `:insecure-directory`).
     KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_DIR names it, else DIR when given, else the host's
     default <tmpdir>/amu-verdict-cache-<euid>; creating the default is part
     of opening it."
     [dir :string] :string
     (if (= "off" (env/read "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE"))
       ""
       (let [configured (env/read "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_DIR")
             chosen (if (> (string-byte-length dir) 0)
                      dir
                      (if (> (string-byte-length configured) 0) configured (default-dir)))]
         (if (absent? chosen)
           (if (= 1 (make-private-directory! chosen))
             (if (secure-dir? chosen) chosen "")
             "")
           (if (secure-dir? chosen) chosen ""))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- entry-path [dir :string key :string] :string
     (posix-path/join dir (string-concat key ".edn"))))

;; :absent, :unreadable (a symlink), :foreign (not a regular file of ours, or
;; group/world writable), or :ok.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- entry-state [file :string] :keyword
     (let [st (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat file "NOFOLLOW_SEP")))]
       (if (< (vector-count st) 4)
         :absent
         (if (= 2 (vector-at st 3))
           :unreadable
           (let [who (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat file "OWNER_SEP")))]
             (if (and (= 0 (vector-at st 3))
                      (>= (vector-count who) 2)
                      (= (vector-at who 0) (vector-at who 1))
                      (not (writable-by-others? (vector-at st 0))))
               :ok
               :foreign)))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- admitted-verdict? [verdict :document] :bool
     (document-equal? verdict (document-edn-read "{:admitted true}"))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- refused-verdict? [verdict :document] :bool
     (and (= :map (document-kind verdict))
          (= 1 (document-count verdict))
          (document-contains verdict (document-keyword :refused))
          (= :map (document-kind (field verdict :refused)))
          (document-contains (field verdict :refused) (document-keyword :message))
          (= :string (document-kind (field (field verdict :refused) :message))))))

;; The record, checked as the host does: closed keys, format, key == requested
;; key == key recomputed from the material, digest, verdict shape.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- record-ok? [record :document key :string] :bool
     (and (= :map (document-kind record))
          (= 5 (document-count record))
          (document-contains record (document-keyword :format))
          (document-contains record (document-keyword :key))
          (document-contains record (document-keyword :key-material))
          (document-contains record (document-keyword :verdict))
          (document-contains record (document-keyword :digest))
          (document-equal? (field record :format) (document-keyword :kotoba.verdict-cache/v1))
          (document-equal? (field record :key) (document-string key))
          (document-equal? (document-string (key-for (field record :key-material))) (document-string key))
          (document-equal? (field record :digest)
                           (document-string (record-digest key (field record :key-material) (field record :verdict))))
          (or (admitted-verdict? (field record :verdict))
              (refused-verdict? (field record :verdict))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- pop-expected [v :vector-i64] :vector-i64
     (let [n (vector-count v)]
       (loop [i 0 out (vector-i64)]
         (if (>= i (- n 1)) out (recur (+ i 1) (vector-conj out (vector-at v i))))))))

;; The language's EDN reader traps on a malformed text, and a raise cannot be
;; caught here, so a record is first checked to be one bracket-balanced form
;; with terminated strings, no reader dispatch (`#`), no comment and no
;; character literal outside a string (a record the host writes has none).
;; `kotoba.lang.edn/read-document` is not used: it keeps every token in a
;; document vector, which the language bounds at 32 items, and a record has
;; far more tokens than that. An odd-length map or a duplicate key is the one
;; malformed shape this does not see; only a writer with this uid could
;; produce it, since the directory and the entry are owner-only.
#?(:kotoba
   (defn- only-space-from? [bs :bytes i :i64] :bool
     (if (>= i (bytes-count bs))
       true
       (let [c (bytes-at bs i)]
         (if (or (= c 32) (= c 10) (= c 13) (= c 9))
           (only-space-from? bs (+ i 1))
           false)))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- balanced-from? [bs :bytes i :i64 stack :vector-i64 in-string :bool escaped :bool] :bool
     (if (>= i (bytes-count bs))
       (if in-string false (= 0 (vector-count stack)))
       (let [c (bytes-at bs i)]
         (if in-string
           (if escaped
             (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack true false)
             (if (= c 92)
               (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack true true)
               (if (= c 34)
                 (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack false false)
                 (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack true false))))
           (if (= c 34)
             (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack true false)
             (if (or (= c 35) (= c 59) (= c 92))
               false
               (if (or (= c 40) (= c 91) (= c 123))
                 (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1)
                                 (vector-conj stack (if (= c 40) 41 (if (= c 91) 93 125))) false false)
                 (if (or (= c 41) (= c 93) (= c 125))
                   (if (= 0 (vector-count stack))
                     false
                     (if (= c (vector-at stack (- (vector-count stack) 1)))
                       (if (= 1 (vector-count stack))
                         (only-space-from? bs (+ i 1))
                         (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) (pop-expected stack) false false))
                       false))
                   (balanced-from? bs (+ i 1) stack false false))))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- one-map-form? [text :string] :bool
     (and (> (string-byte-length text) 1)
          (= 123 (string-code-point-at text 0))
          (balanced-from? (string-to-utf8 text) 0 (vector-i64) false false))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn- checked-verdict [text :string key :string] :document
     (if (one-map-form? text)
       (let [record (document-edn-read text)]
         (if (record-ok? record key) (field record :verdict) (document-null)))
       (document-null))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn lookup-verdict
     "The trusted verdict stored under KEY in DIR (`{:admitted true}` or
     `{:refused ...}`), or null: a miss. An entry that is a symlink, foreign,
     malformed, or whose key/digest do not verify is deleted and is a miss."
     [dir :string key :string] :document
     (if (= 0 (string-byte-length dir))
       (document-null)
       (let [file (entry-path dir key)
             state (entry-state file)]
         (if (= state :absent)
           (document-null)
           (if (= state :ok)
             (let [size (vector-at (numbers (fs/app-data (string-concat file "NOFOLLOW_SEP"))) 1)
                   verdict (checked-verdict (fs/app-data (string-concat file (string-concat "RANGE_SEP0:" (string-from-i64 size)))) key)]
               (if (= :null (document-kind verdict))
                 (do (fs/app-data (string-concat file "UNLINK_SEP")) (document-null))
                 verdict))
             (do (fs/app-data (string-concat file "UNLINK_SEP")) (document-null))))))))

#?(:kotoba
   (defn store-verdict!
     "Write the record for KEY: an empty 0600 temporary (O_NOFOLLOW), CHMOD,
     the record, RENAME -- no byte exists under another mode. Answers 1 when
     stored, 0 when not (the cache is an optimization: a failed write loses
     the entry, never the verdict). The temporary is always removed."
     [dir :string key :string material :document verdict :document] :i64
     (if (= 0 (string-byte-length dir))
       0
       (let [file (entry-path dir key)
             empty (document-edn-read "{}")
             record (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc (assoc empty :format (document-keyword :kotoba.verdict-cache/v1))
                                                :key (document-string key))
                                         :key-material material)
                                  :verdict verdict)
                           :digest (document-string (record-digest key material verdict)))
             content (string-concat (document-edn-print record) "\n")
             temporary (string-concat file (string-concat "." (string-concat (entropy/draw "16") ".tmp")))
             created (fs/app-data (string-concat temporary "WRITE_SEP"))
             chmod (fs/app-data (string-concat temporary (string-concat "CHMOD_SEP" "600")))
             written (if (= "1" chmod) (fs/app-data (string-concat temporary (string-concat "WRITE_SEP" content))) "")
             moved (if (= "1" chmod) (fs/app-data (string-concat temporary (string-concat "RENAME_SEP" file))) "0")
             removed (fs/app-data (string-concat temporary "UNLINK_SEP"))]
         (if (= "1" moved) 1 0)))))

#?(:kotoba
   nil
   :default
   (do
(def ^:private record-format :kotoba.verdict-cache/v1)
(def ^:private key-format :kotoba.verdict-key/v1)

;; Octal literals do not read on nbb; these are 0o022 and 0o600.
(def ^:private group-or-world-writable 18)
(def ^:private private-file-mode "600")

(def ^:private windows? #?(:cljs (sys/windows?) :default false))

(defn- configured-integer [#?@(:kotoba [name :string default :i64 maximum :i64] :default [name default maximum])]
  #?@(:kotoba [:i64] :default [])
  (let [text (env/read name)]
    ;; Kotoba: an unset or non-decimal setting is the default, as nbb's
    ;; `js/Number.isSafeInteger` check makes it; `decimal?` admits 1-18 digits
    ;; with an optional sign, which are all safe integers.
    #?(:kotoba (if (and (decimal-text/decimal? text)
                        (<= 1 (decimal-text/parse text))
                        (<= (decimal-text/parse text) maximum))
                 (decimal-text/parse text)
                 default)
       :default (let [value (when (seq text) (js/Number text))]
                  (if (and value (js/Number.isSafeInteger value) (<= 1 value maximum))
                    value
                    default)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; wire-35 answers

(defn- fields
  "The decimal fields of a STAT / NOFOLLOW / OWNER answer; nil when absent."
  [answer]
  (when (seq answer)
    (decimal-text/fields answer)))

(defn- nofollow [p] (fields (fs/app-data (str p "NOFOLLOW_SEP"))))
(defn- stat [p] (fields (fs/app-data (str p "STAT_SEP"))))

(defn- owned?
  "The final component of P (not followed) belongs to this process's euid."
  [p]
  (let [[owner me] (fields (fs/app-data (str p "OWNER_SEP")))]
    (boolean (and owner (= owner me)))))

(defn- own-uid []
  (second (fields (fs/app-data (str "/" "OWNER_SEP")))))

(defn- listing
  "The names in DIR, sorted bytewise (fs/browse)."
  [dir]
  (let [answer (fs/browse dir)]
    (if (= "" answer)
      []
      (mapv #(first (text/split % #"\t")) (text/split answer #"\n")))))

(defn- spelled [p] (if windows? (text/replace p "\\" "/") p))

(defn- absolute?
  [p]
  (or (text/starts-with? p "/")
      (and windows? (boolean (re-matches #"[A-Za-z]:/.*|//.*" p)))))

(defn- resolve-path
  "P made absolute against the working directory (sys/cwd), normalized, with
  no trailing slash -- node:path resolve's answer on POSIX."
  [p]
  (let [p (spelled p)
        joined (posix-path/normalize
                (if (absolute? p) p (posix-path/join (spelled (sys/cwd "")) p)))]
    (if (and (< 1 (count joined)) (text/ends-with? joined "/"))
      (subs joined 0 (dec (count joined)))
      joined)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Toolchain and limits identity

(defn- file-digest [file]
  (hash/sha256 (fs/app-data-bytes file)))

(defn- files-under
  "[relative-path absolute-path] of every regular file under DIR, in bytewise
  name order, depth first."
  [dir]
  (let [out (volatile! [])]
    (letfn [(walk [d rel]
              (doseq [entry (listing d)]
                (let [p (str d "/" entry)
                      r (if (= "" rel) entry (str rel "/" entry))
                      kind (nth (nofollow p) 3 nil)]
                  (cond (= 1 kind) (walk p r)
                        (= 0 kind) (vswap! out conj [r p])
                        ;; A symlink inside a hashed tree is refused rather
                        ;; than followed or skipped: either would let the
                        ;; digest say less than what was loaded.
                        :else (throw (ex-info "toolchain tree contains a non-regular file"
                                              {:path p}))))))]
      (walk dir ""))
    @out))

(defn- pinned-gitlib? [entry]
  ;; `.../.gitlibs/libs/<group>/<artifact>/<40-hex sha>/...`: the path names
  ;; the commit, which is the identity deps-lock.edn pins.
  (boolean (re-find #"[/\\]\.gitlibs[/\\]libs[/\\].+[/\\][0-9a-f]{40}([/\\]|$)" entry)))

(defn- argv-classpath []
  (let [argv #?(:cljs (sys/argv) :default [])
        i (first (keep-indexed (fn [i a] (when (= "--classpath" a) i)) argv))]
    (when (and (some? i) (< (inc i) (count argv)))
      (let [cp (nth argv (inc i))
            delimiter #?(:cljs (sys/path-delimiter) :default ":")]
        (vec (remove #(= "" %)
                         ;; Kotoba: a regex literal is refused by name, and the
                         ;; delimiter is a plain string here, so it is the separator.
                         #?(:kotoba (text/split cp delimiter)
                            :default (text/split cp (re-pattern (text/re-quote delimiter))))))))))

(defn- compute-toolchain-digest
  ;; v2 (2026-09-25): the digest of a text that names every file by its own
  ;; sha256, where v1 streamed the file bytes into one hash. The hash/sha256
  ;; ability answers one value per call; the inputs the digest covers are
  ;; the same, and the tag moved so no v1 key is read under v2.
  [entries]
  (let [parts (volatile! [(str "kotoba.verdict-toolchain/v2\u0000"
                               #?(:cljs (sys/runtime-version) :default "kotoba") "\u0000"
                               (pr-str compatibility/compiler-version) "\u0000")])]
    (doseq [entry entries]
      (let [absolute (resolve-path entry)
            [_ _ _ is-dir] (stat absolute)]
        (vswap! parts conj (str "entry\u0000" absolute "\u0000"))
        (cond
          (pinned-gitlib? absolute) (vswap! parts conj "pinned\u0000")
          (nil? is-dir) (vswap! parts conj "absent\u0000")
          (= 0 is-dir) (vswap! parts conj (str "sha256\u0000" (file-digest absolute) "\u0000"))
          :else (doseq [[rel file] (files-under absolute)]
                  (vswap! parts conj (str "file\u0000" rel "\u0000" (file-digest file) "\u0000"))))))
    (hash/sha256 (apply str @parts))))

(def ^:private toolchain-memo (volatile! nil))

(defn toolchain-digest
  "`{:digest hex}` or `{:unavailable reason}`. Computed once per process from
  the classpath the process was started with. No classpath on argv means no
  identity for the code that would produce the verdict, and therefore no
  cache -- never a cache keyed on less."
  ([] (or @toolchain-memo
          (vreset! toolchain-memo
                   (if-let [entries (argv-classpath)]
                     (toolchain-digest entries)
                     {:unavailable :no-classpath-on-argv}))))
  ([entries]
   (try {:digest (compute-toolchain-digest entries) :entries entries}
        (catch :default e
          {:unavailable :toolchain-unreadable :message (ex-message e)}))))

(defn limits-digest
  "sha256 of the first `kotoba/lang/limits.edn` found on ENTRIES (the
  vendored copy of kotoba-lang `lang/limits.edn` that `kotoba.compiler.limits`
  is checked against). nil when none is found."
  [entries]
  (some (fn [entry]
          (let [file (posix-path/join (spelled entry) "kotoba/lang/limits.edn")]
            (when (= "1" (fs/app-data (str file "EXISTS_SEP")))
              (file-digest file))))
        entries))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Keys and records

(def ^:private key-fields
  [:definitions :subject :toolchain :target :capabilities :limits])

(defn key-material
  "The ordered vector the key is the hash of. Every field is present, named,
  and in a fixed order; a nil field is part of the material, not omitted."
  [kind fields]
  [key-format kind (mapv (fn [k] [k (get fields k)]) key-fields)])

(defn key-for [material] (artifact/sha256 material))

(defn record-digest [key material verdict]
  (artifact/sha256 [record-format key material verdict]))

(defn- refusal-verdict [error]
  {:refused {:message (ex-message error) :data (ex-data error)}})

(defn- replayable? [verdict]
  ;; A verdict whose text does not read back as the same value cannot be
  ;; replayed as the same diagnostic, so it is not stored.
  ;; Read back with the same reader `check-record` uses, so what is stored is
  ;; exactly what can be read. kotoba.lang.edn since 2026-09-25 (cljs.reader
  ;; before; superproject adr-2609242330): it is bounded and refuses tags,
  ;; integers beyond 2^53-1 and `#_`, so a verdict carrying one is now not
  ;; stored -- a miss, never a different verdict.
  (try (= verdict (edn/read-string (pr-str verdict)))
       (catch :default _ false)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The store

(defn- secure-directory? [dir]
  (let [[mode _ _ kind] (nofollow dir)]
    (when (nil? kind)
      (throw (ex-info "verdict cache directory is absent" {:dir dir})))
    (and (= 1 kind)
         (or windows?
             (and (owned? dir)
                  (zero? (bit-and mode group-or-world-writable)))))))

(defn- directory? [p]
  (= 1 (nth (stat p) 3 nil)))

(defn- make-private-directory!
  "Create DIR (and any missing parent) as a 0700 directory: MKTEMP in the
  parent -- created 0700 by the host -- then RENAME to DIR, so DIR never
  exists with a wider mode. A DIR another run created meanwhile is used."
  [dir]
  (let [parent (posix-path/dirname dir)]
    (when (and (not= parent dir) (nil? (stat parent)))
      (make-private-directory! parent))
    (let [staged (fs/app-data (str parent "MKTEMP_SEP" ".amu-verdict-cache-"))]
      (when (= "" staged)
        (throw (ex-info "verdict cache directory could not be created" {:dir dir})))
      (when-not (= "1" (fs/app-data (str staged "RENAME_SEP" dir)))
        (fs/app-data (str staged "RMDIR_SEP"))
        (when-not (directory? dir)
          (throw (ex-info "verdict cache directory could not be created" {:dir dir})))))))

(defn- tmpdir []
  #?(:cljs (sys/tmpdir)
     :default (let [t (some #(let [v (env/read %)] (when (seq v) v)) ["TMPDIR" "TMP" "TEMP"])
                    t (or t "/tmp")]
                (if (and (< 1 (count t)) (text/ends-with? t "/")) (subs t 0 (dec (count t))) t))))

(defn open-store
  "`{:dir ...}` or `{:disabled reason}`. Creating the default directory is
  part of opening it; an existing directory with the wrong owner or mode
  disables the cache rather than being repaired."
  ([] (open-store {}))
  ([{:keys [dir]}]
   (cond
     (= "off" (env/read "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE"))
     {:disabled :off}

     :else
     (let [configured (env/read "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_DIR")
           dir (or dir
                   (when (seq configured) configured)
                   (posix-path/join (spelled (tmpdir))
                                    (str "amu-verdict-cache-" (if windows? "w" (own-uid)))))]
       (try
         (when (nil? (stat dir))
           (make-private-directory! dir))
         (if (secure-directory? dir)
           {:dir dir
            :max-entries (configured-integer "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_ENTRIES" 4096 65536)
            :max-bytes (configured-integer "KOTOBA_VERDICT_CACHE_BYTES"
                                           (* 16 1024 1024) (* 1024 1024 1024))}
           {:disabled :insecure-directory :dir dir})
         (catch :default e
           {:disabled :directory-unavailable :dir dir :message (ex-message e)}))))))

(defn- entry-path [store key] (posix-path/join (:dir store) (str key ".edn")))

(defn- read-protected [file]
  ;; nil when absent; throws a named problem when present but not ours.
  (if windows?
    (let [[_ _ _ is-dir] (stat file)]
      (cond
        (nil? is-dir) nil
        (not= 0 is-dir) (throw (ex-info "foreign" {:reason :foreign-entry}))
        :else (try (fs/app-data file)
                   (catch :default _ (throw (ex-info "unreadable" {:reason :unreadable}))))))
    (let [[mode size _ kind] (nofollow file)]
      (cond
        (nil? kind) nil
        (= 2 kind) (throw (ex-info "unreadable" {:reason :unreadable}))
        (not (and (= 0 kind) (owned? file)
                  (zero? (bit-and mode group-or-world-writable))))
        (throw (ex-info "foreign" {:reason :foreign-entry}))
        :else (try (fs/app-data (str file "RANGE_SEP0:" size))
                   (catch :default _ (throw (ex-info "unreadable" {:reason :unreadable}))))))))

(defn- check-record [text key]
  ;; kotoba.lang.edn refuses every tagged literal with no options, which is
  ;; what the `{:readers {} :default <throw>}` pair told cljs.reader to do.
  (let [record (try (edn/read-string text)
                    (catch :default _ ::unreadable))]
    (cond
      (= ::unreadable record) {:reason :unreadable}
      (not (and (map? record) (= record-format (:format record))
                (= #{:format :key :key-material :verdict :digest} (set (keys record)))))
      {:reason :malformed}
      (not= key (:key record)) {:reason :key-mismatch}
      (not= key (key-for (:key-material record))) {:reason :key-material-mismatch}
      (not= (:digest record)
            (record-digest key (:key-material record) (:verdict record)))
      {:reason :digest-mismatch}
      (not (or (= {:admitted true} (:verdict record))
               (and (map? (:refused (:verdict record)))
                    (string? (get-in record [:verdict :refused :message])))))
      {:reason :malformed}
      :else {:verdict (:verdict record)})))

(defn- evict! [store]
  (let [dir (:dir store)
        entries (->> (listing dir)
                     (filter #(re-matches #"[0-9a-f]{64}\.edn" %))
                     (keep (fn [n] (let [p (posix-path/join dir n)
                                         [_ size] (stat p)
                                         mtime (fs/app-data (str p "MTIME_SEP"))]
                                     (when (and size (seq mtime))
                                       {:path p :size size :mtime (decimal-text/parse mtime)}))))
                     (sort-by :mtime))]
    (loop [entries entries
           n (count entries)
           bytes (reduce + 0 (map :size entries))]
      (when (and (seq entries)
                 (or (> n (:max-entries store)) (> bytes (:max-bytes store))))
        (fs/app-data (str (:path (first entries)) "UNLINK_SEP"))
        (recur (rest entries) (dec n) (- bytes (:size (first entries))))))))

(defn- write-record! [store key material verdict]
  (let [file (entry-path store key)
        content (str (pr-str {:format record-format :key key :key-material material
                              :verdict verdict
                              :digest (record-digest key material verdict)})
                     "\n")
        temporary (str file "." (entropy/draw "16") ".tmp")]
    (when (<= (text-bytes/utf8-length content) (:max-bytes store))
      (try
        ;; Created empty (O_NOFOLLOW), made 0600, and only then written.
        (fs/app-data (str temporary "WRITE_SEP"))
        (when-not (= "1" (fs/app-data (str temporary "CHMOD_SEP" private-file-mode)))
          (throw (ex-info "chmod" {})))
        (fs/app-data (str temporary "WRITE_SEP" content))
        (when-not (= "1" (fs/app-data (str temporary "RENAME_SEP" file)))
          (throw (ex-info "rename" {})))
        (evict! store)
        (catch :default _
          ;; The cache is an optimization: a failed write loses the entry,
          ;; never the verdict.
          nil)
        (finally (fs/app-data (str temporary "UNLINK_SEP")))))))

(defn- default-warn [message]
  (io/write-error (str message "\n")))

(defn- answer
  "Return or throw what VERDICT says, identically for a fresh and a replayed
  refusal: same message, same ex-data (so the same exit code)."
  [verdict result]
  (if-let [refused (:refused verdict)]
    (throw (ex-info (:message refused) (:data refused)))
    result))

(defn resolve!
  "Answer the static verdict of KIND for FIELDS, computing it with COMPUTE only
  when no trusted entry exists. COMPUTE returns normally for admitted and
  throws for refused. Returns `{:cache status :key k}` on an admitted verdict
  (status one of :hit :miss :rejected :disabled :unkeyed; :rejected carries
  :reason) and rethrows the refusal otherwise.

  FIELDS carries :definitions :subject :target :capabilities; the store
  supplies :toolchain and :limits unless FIELDS already names them (tests)."
  [store kind fields compute & {:keys [warn]}]
  (let [warn (or warn default-warn)
        toolchain (if (contains? fields :toolchain)
                    {:digest (:toolchain fields)}
                    (toolchain-digest))
        limits (if (contains? fields :limits)
                 (:limits fields)
                 (some-> (:entries toolchain) limits-digest))
        run-fresh (fn []
                    (try (compute) {:admitted true}
                         (catch :default e
                           (if (ex-data e) (refusal-verdict e) (throw e)))))]
    (cond
      (:disabled store)
      (answer (run-fresh) {:cache :disabled :reason (:disabled store)})

      (nil? (:definitions fields))
      (answer (run-fresh) {:cache :unkeyed :reason :no-definition-identity})

      (not (:digest toolchain))
      (answer (run-fresh) {:cache :unkeyed :reason (:unavailable toolchain)})

      (nil? limits)
      (answer (run-fresh) {:cache :unkeyed :reason :no-limits-table})

      :else
      (let [material (key-material kind (assoc fields
                                               :toolchain (:digest toolchain)
                                               :limits limits))
            key (key-for material)
            file (entry-path store key)
            found (try (some-> (read-protected file) (check-record key))
                       (catch :default e {:reason (or (:reason (ex-data e)) :unreadable)}))]
        (if-let [verdict (:verdict found)]
          (answer verdict {:cache :hit :key key})
          (let [rejected (:reason found)
                _ (when rejected
                    (fs/app-data (str file "UNLINK_SEP"))
                    (warn (str "kotoba.verdict-cache: rejected entry " key
                               " (" (name rejected) "); recomputed")))
                verdict (run-fresh)]
            (when (replayable? verdict)
              (write-record! store key material verdict))
            (answer verdict (cond-> {:cache (if rejected :rejected :miss) :key key}
                              rejected (assoc :reason rejected)))))))))))
